               </text>
            </section>
            <section>
               <title value="Hospital course note"/>
               <code>
                  <coding>
                     <system value="http://loinc.org"/>
                     <code value="8648-8"/>
                     <display value="Hospital course note"/>
                  </coding>
               </code>
               <text>
                  <status value="generated"/>
                  <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the hospital admission of your 88-year-old female patient from 12th to 13th August 1991. She was admitted due to an acute exacerbation of her known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, she presented with increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced oxygen saturation. Physical examination, chest X-ray, arterial blood gas analysis, and pulse oximetry confirmed the exacerbation. Blood tests were performed to exclude infection and assess metabolic status. The patient was treated with nebulised bronchodilators, systemic corticosteroids, and supplemental oxygen therapy. Vital signs were monitored closely throughout the stay. She responded satisfactorily to treatment with improvement in respiratory function. She is discharged in stable condition. I recommend continued bronchodilator therapy and close outpatient follow-up. Please do not hesitate to contact me with any questions. Yours sincerely, Dr. [Hospital Physician]</div>
               </text>
            </section>
